    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 80574,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/0/80574.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think a lot of their energy is because we all remember it was a week ago, two weeks ago, they were in complete and utter chaos. They were despondent. They were dejected. They really looked defeated. And at that point, they had made their internal calculation that they had to push Joe Biden out. So obviously they're kind of having a euphoria moment, but that's not going to last because the campaign is going to have to now move into high gear. I've had an opportunity to listen to Kamala Harris on the stump the last couple days. She hasn't really said anything. It's platitudes. It's kind of a rewashed Barack Obama, Bill Clinton type of speech. But there's no new ideas. There's no new strategies of how she's going to move the country forward. It's this constant a political trope from the left of, we're not going back, we're going forward. But that doesn't mean anything, especially considering the fact that Donald Trump has been president of the United States. And when he was president, our country was more prosperous. Every demographic group was more prosperous. Our country was secure. Our foreign policy was in the best shape it had been in a generation.",
