  {
    "episode_id": 80574,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/0/80574.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "Well, listen, obviously, Kamala Harris is going to try to campaign on abortion. It's the one issue that the Democrats seem to be leading and polling as it stands right now. But the facts of today in America are that every state's going to make this decision. It is no longer just been decided by the Supreme Court in the most undemocratic process I might add, because that's what happened in 1973 with Roe v. Wade. The Supreme Court just took the issue away from the hands of the American people. Now our democracy, now our republic is going to go through the political process and make a determination state by state of how abortion is going to be managed and treated going forward. In California, in New York, in Illinois, they already have their abortion law. They're very likely not to make any changes. In Iowa, in Tennessee, in Florida, we have a ballot initiative on our ballot. Same thing that happened in Ohio. Every state is making that decision. So what you're witnessing on abortion, now that Roe v. Wade has been overturned, is that people are now making their voices heard. But for a Kamala Harris to campaign on it, like she can do something on abortion is not factual, is not accurate, and quite frankly is gaslighting. Because the Dobbs decision is very clear, the federal government has no role in abortion, it's now going to be left to the states.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_04",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "The federal government has no role in abortion policy after the Dobbs decision.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "All U.S. states will decide abortion policy independently after the overturning of Roe v. Wade.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "Kamala Harris will attempt to campaign on abortion.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The Supreme Court previously removed abortion decisions from the public via the 1973 Roe v. Wade ruling.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
